+/*
+ * LIUQIN touchscreen: Novatek NT36532 on GENI SPI4.
+ *
+ * The panel's touch controller is a Novatek NT36532 on GENI SPI4 (QUPv3
+ * wrapper 0, serial engine 4, spi@0x990000), chip select 0, with its
+ * interrupt on TLMM gpio21 and the data/clock pins on gpio16..gpio19 in
+ * function "qup4".  Facts from the mainline tree this port follows
+ * (yzddmr6/linux-sm8450-liuqin, branch liuqin-6.17, sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
+ * and sm8450.dtsi, which in turn quotes the vendor bootloader's FDT).
+ *
+ * Boot arg liuqintouch:
+ *   0 off (default), 1 read-only audit, 2 + clocks and pin mux,
+ *   3 + SPI master, Novatek trim id and the 10-finger report thread.
+ *
+ * Stages 1 and 2 never touch a register that the previous stage did not
+ * prove reachable: serial engine registers are only accessed when the GCC
+ * side says the engine's clocks are running, because an access to a gated
+ * QUP block hangs the bus.
+ *
+ * Stage 3 programs the SE the way drivers/spi/spi-geni-qcom.c does in
+ * spi_geni_init() and setup_fifo_params(): geni_se_init(), FIFO mode, 8-bit
+ * words with byte packing, SPI mode 0, chip select 0, and the SE clock
+ * (BI_TCXO, 19.2 MHz, no prescaler) divided down by GENI_SER_M_CLK_CFG.
+ * Transfers are polled FIFO transfers, with chip select driven by hand
+ * (SPI_CS_ASSERT / SPI_CS_DEASSERT), because there is no SPI core here.
+ *
+ * Optional stage-3 boot args, all for on-device debugging:
+ *   liuqintouchdiv=N    SE clock divider, SCLK = 19.2 MHz / N (default 16,
+ *                       i.e. 1.2 MHz; the part is rated for 9.6 MHz)
+ *   liuqintouchpoll=1   read the event buffer every tick instead of waiting
+ *                       for gpio21 to assert
+ *   liuqintouchswap=1   exchange the controller's x and y
+ *   liuqintouchflip=N   bit 0 mirrors x, bit 1 mirrors y
+ */
